diff --git a/docs/design-changes.md b/docs/design-changes.md
index 15875f2..fe39241 100644
--- a/docs/design-changes.md
+++ b/docs/design-changes.md
@@ -19,3 +19,5 @@ Stage 12 sketch (design, not a screenshot): title and profile at top; race field
 Before stage 13: extend the simple window with a circuit panel. Add track.py for pure geometry: fit normalised vertices inside a padded rectangle with one scale factor, retain aspect ratio and close the route explicitly for drawing. Tests will check all profiles and bounds; no moving marker until stage 14. The larger working canvas is an intermediate layout, not the final timing-console refinement.
 
 Before stage 14: add replay.py because a shared elapsed-time clock and lap lookup are separate from drawing. Both cars use the same elapsed seconds, but each uses its own cumulative lap boundaries. Interpolate by distance along the closed schematic. The replay is a timing illustration; it does not model corner speed or a pit-lane path. Duration is the slower plan total, so one car may finish earlier. Clamp scrubbing to 0-1, stop at the end, restart paused at zero, and reset after successful simulation/profile changes. Keep the last valid replay when input validation fails.
+
+Before stage 15: storage.py will own a versioned Session record containing exactly two plans, two pace offsets, selected profile key, race values and Conditions. JSON is parsed strictly (duplicate keys/non-finite constants rejected), bounded to 100 KB, and validated before a UI state change. Save and CSV export write a unique sibling temporary file and replace the chosen destination only after completion. Cleanup removes only the temporary file created by this call. GUI file pickers use the standard-library Tk dialog; cancellation leaves state unchanged. Export recomputes the current valid configuration so stale displayed results cannot leak into a new export. CSV includes plan identifier and all additive lap components with three-decimal numeric output.
